pl="N"/></sources></patcit><patcit ucid="JP-9207276-A" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>JP</country><doc-number>9207276</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="A" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit><patcit ucid="JP-9317142-A" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>JP</country><doc-number>9317142</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="A" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit></patent-citations><non-patent-citations><nplcit status="new"><text>See also references of EP     1041110A1</text><sources><source name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></nplcit></non-patent-citations></citations></technical-data><parties><applicants><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>INADA TOSHIAKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>NITTO BOSEKI CO LTD</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>INADA, TOSHIAKI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NITTO BOSEKI CO., LTD.</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>INADA TOSHIAKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>INADA, TOSHIAKI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>An interior resin article which comprises 10 to 45 parts by weight of an ethylene-vinyl acetate copolymer having a vinyl acetate content of 50 % or more, 55 to 90 wt.% of a polyolefin resin and 100 to 700 parts by weight of an inorganic filler, wherein the ethylene-vinyl acetate copolymer has a melt flow rate (MFR) being higher than that of the polyolefin resin by 20 g/10 min or more. This article provides an interior resin article which contains no halogen or phthalate ester plasticizer, exhibits characteristics equivalent to those of PVC resin articles with respect to resistance to scratching, design flexibility, fabricability and the like, and, in particular, has excellent adhesion with conventional interior adhesives.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention se rapporte à un article d'intérieur en résine qui comporte 10 à 45 parties en poids d'un copolymère éthylène acétate de vinyle ayant une proportion d'acétate de vinyle supérieure ou égale à 50 %, 55 à 90 % en poids d'une résine de polyoléfine et 100 à 700 parts en poids d'une charge inorganique, ledit copolymère éthylène acétate de vinyle possédant un coefficient de fluidité (MFR melt flow rate) supérieur à celui d'une résine de polyoléfine d'au moins 20 g/10 min. Cet article constitue un article d'intérieur en résine qui ne contient aucun plastifiant à base d'ester de phtalate ou d'halogène, qui présente des caractéristiques équivalentes à celles des articles en résine PVC en ce qui concerne la résistance aux égratignures, la souplesse de conception, la facilité de fabrication et analogues, et qui notamment présente un excellent pouvoir d'adhésion aux adhésifs d'intérieur classiques.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>